(96271, 3841, 1005, '<td valign="top">I like the title, don''t quite get it, but thinking isn''t my strong suit.  Photographically, it''s an odd mix of too dark, with some too bright spots, like the end of the knife handle.  (Until has just one L, I think)  Shine more light directly on the $20, in line with the knife, that should still display the knife, and show off the bill more.    Was the Martha Stewart label an manufactured prop?  I still haven''t figured out how to light the label, the knife and the money without hurting one of them.  5 Swash</td>', 'I like the title, don''t quite get it, but thinking isn''t my strong suit.  Photographically, it''s an odd mix of too dark, with some too bright spots, like the end of the knife handle.  (Until has just one L, I think)  Shine more light directly on the $20, in line with the knife, that should still display the knife, and show off the bill more.    Was the Martha Stewart label an manufactured prop?  I still haven''t figured out how to light the label, the knife and the money without hurting one of them.  5 Swash', '2002-07-29 19:59:00.000000', NULL, 1),
